{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491706-errata-or-just-an-update-needed-for-changing-ways","id":1491706,"title":"Errata or just an update needed for Changing Ways","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-28T19:55:21-07:00","id":1491706,"title":"Errata or just an update needed for Changing Ways","content":"Hello, after some readings and readings I found this on page 132 of the Changing Ways book (second text column):<br /> <br /> <i>Another takes part in a sacred hunt. <b>Spirits cross the<br /> Gauntlet to possess exemplary spirits </b>or powerful people<br /> in the physical world<b>.</b> By sniffing out such a creature, the<br /> werewolf drives her pack to hunt it down so that she may<br /> kill it and consume its power. A Gaffling may only provide<br /> a gift of Gnosis, while a more powerful spirit may grant a<br /> Gift in return. The hunt itself is chiminage: proving that<br /> the werewolf is a skilled enough hunter to track down<br /> creatures from the spirit world in the physical. Though<br /> they do not take place in the Umbra, such hunts often<br /> see the pack faced with symbols and challenges related to<br /> the spirit\u2019s nature.</i><br /> <br /> Is there any errata or update available? Or am I just crazy in seeing a mistake in the bold part? Can I get help from the community to get the OP team to correct this possible mistake?<br /> Thank you for your time and attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T00:15:02-07:00","id":1491717,"title":"","content":"It's highly unlikely to get fixed. Paradox is pushing Onyx Path to stop doing 20th books, and many of the last few W20 books had a lot of behind the scenes drama.<br /> <br /> W20 Changing Ways was probably the worse in this regard, with the line/book developer having gone on record at getting so fed up with notes from WW/Paradox that he essentially phoned in the book to get it good enough to be published so his team could get paid for their work before he quit making RPGs and move on with his life. I doubt there's much energy at Onyx Path to revisit it at this pint.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}